# PatternFly 6 Migration Rules for Foreman Plugin

## Documentation

Always reference these files when generating or editing PatternFly code:
- `AGENT.md` — project-specific migration guide
- `.claude/instructions/pf6-migration-patterns.md` — before/after code recipes
- `.claude/instructions/pf6-testing-recipes.md` — PF6 test patterns

## Import Rules

- NEVER import from `@patternfly/react-core/deprecated`
- NEVER import from `@patternfly/react-core/next`
- NEVER import from `@patternfly/react-table/deprecated`
- NEVER import from `patternfly-react` or `patternfly` (PF3)
- ALWAYS use `@patternfly/react-charts/victory` for chart components
- ALWAYS use `@patternfly/react-core` for all PF components

## CSS Rules

- Use `--pf-t--global--*` semantic design tokens for colors, spacing, fonts
- Use `--pf-v6-c-*` for component-level variable overrides
- NEVER use `pf-v5-` prefixed class names
- NEVER hardcode hex/rgb colors — use PF6 design tokens for dark mode compat

## Component Rules

- ALWAYS use functional components with hooks
- Use `useSelector` and `useDispatch` for Redux (NEVER `connect()`)
- Use `translate as __` from `foremanReact/common/I18n` for all user-visible strings
- Use PF6 composable patterns: Modal(Header+Body+Footer), Dropdown(MenuToggle+DropdownList)

## Testing Rules

- Use React Testing Library (`render`, `screen`, `waitFor`) — NEVER Enzyme
- Query by role first: `screen.getByRole('button', { name: '...' })`
- Use `@testing-library/user-event` for interactions (not `fireEvent`)
- Wrap router-dependent components in `<MemoryRouter>`

## Foreman Plugin Rules

- Shared deps (React, PF, Redux) come from core via Module Federation — do NOT bundle separately
- Import core utils via `foremanReact/` alias (e.g., `foremanReact/common/I18n`)
- Fill components must render PF6 markup to match core UI
